The maximum value would be if an infinite number of new players joined, each one bringing an additional life to the game. In this case:

\boxed{total \ \text{lives} \leq \infty \ \text{(infinite number of lives)}}

So, we cannot provide a single numerical answer for the total number of lives. Instead, the answer is a range representing the minimum and maximum possible values for the total number of lives: \boxed{18 \leq total \text{ lives} \leq \infty}

